<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47221" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">symphōnĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συμφωνία,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an agreement of
				sounds</i>, <i>concord</i>, <i>harmony</i>, <i>symphony.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, sing.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum symphonia caneret,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 44, § 105</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 5, 13, § 31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fam.
				16, 9, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 39, 10, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 8,
				8, § 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 29, 43, §
			84</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. E 12, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. A. P.
				374</span></i>.—<i>Plur.</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Cael.
				15, 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cels. 3, 18 al.</span></i>—Of <i>a signal</i> in war, <i><span class="en">Prud.
				ad Symm. 2, 527</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in late Lat., <i>a
				kind of musical instrument</i>, <i><span class="en">Isid.
				Orig. 3, 22 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; cf.
					<i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 21, 29</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
